The arrival spec now resolves the public folder via `process.cwd()` without `import.meta` or `fileURLToPath`.

Playwright executes spec files in CommonJS mode where `import.meta` triggers a module loader error. Resolving `public` directly via `resolve(process.cwd(), 'public')` keeps the spec compatible with CommonJS execution while dropping the unused `dirname` and `fileURLToPath` imports.

What now works:
The test spec at [arrival.spec.ts](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-arrival/tests/color-polish-scenes/arrival.spec.ts) loads cleanly in Playwright, and the lane record at [arrival.md](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-arrival/docs/runs/2026-09-11-tv-scenes/lanes/arrival.md) records Round 4.

